# uv.lock is generated output, not source. A textual 3-way merge of it produces
# meaningless conflicts (one hunk per bumped transitive version) and, worse, can
# silently yield a lockfile that satisfies no real resolution. Marking it binary
# makes git refuse to merge it at all: any two-sided change becomes a clean
# conflict with our side left in the worktree, which the release script then
# regenerates with `uv lock`. Never resolve this file by hand.
uv.lock merge=binary linguist-generated=true
